        "explanation": "Senators Dodd and Lieberman announce $2,250,000 in federal grants for airport runway improvements in Connecticut, taking direct credit for delivering this physical and financial benefit to their home state."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "A text should NOT be classified as credit-claiming (0) if:\n1. The senator is merely introducing a bill, sponsoring a pending resolution, or co-sponsoring legislation that has not yet passed. This represents position-taking.\n2. The senator is criticizing the administration, discussing ongoing hearings, or expressing an opinion on policy without a finished outcome. This is policy position-taking.\n3. The senator is announcing an upcoming town hall, sending a letter requesting assistance, or receiving a symbolic award. These represent general advertising.",
    "negative_examples": [
      {
